WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:09.730
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:20.370
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.490
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:06.970
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:14.270
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:20.940
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:28.430
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:59.150
I know they say,
“there’s no place like home”…

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:00.970
…but you’re all so comfortable.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:04.210
It looks like some
still have a way to go.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.940
Oh, the young lady with
the charming new hairstyle.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.280
Boo!

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.070
What’s the matter, Roatreamon?

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.570
Well, this bed seems
to be a little lopsided.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.840
It’s not just your imagination, milady?

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:34.980
It’s old.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.550
You can put up with that much.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.680
But it really bothers me.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.180
It creaks if I move
just a little, and that bothers me.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:46.910
Hold this.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.090
Do you think you can…

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.400
Here goes…

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:04.410
Hurry up…

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.920
How’s that?

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.250
You fixed it.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.730
Thank you, Mamina.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:17.000
Don’t thank me
for something like this.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.300
What’s with them?

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.520
Who knows?
Something to do with that haircut?

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.310
We’re descending.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.770
Have we reached our destination?

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:54.380
We’ve stopped.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:09.640
<b>United Front</b>

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:23.190
Man, what a piece of junk.
Where’s the bridge?

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:27.860
This is the priestesses’ ship?
I imagined something better.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.720
Like a secret garden?

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.040
Hey, look.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.610
Those are sibyllae?

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.250
This is the first time I’ve seen one.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.380
Hey, you! Quit socializing.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.500
Let’s go.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.350
What’s going on here?

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.280
This ship has Simoun
sibyllae on board…

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:56.350
We know. That’s why we
went out of our way to join you.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:57.350
Out of your way?

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.160
Perfect timing.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.860
Can you take me to the bridge?

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:05.630
I won’t allow
such disrespect! We are…

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.360
If you please… Come this way.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.320
Yun.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.370
Just a minute.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:11.950
I will show them the way.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.770
This way.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:14.870
Neviril.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.450
Wait here, guys.

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:17.560
Gotcha.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.010
Just as you’d expect from Neviril.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:33.530
Welcome to the Messis. First of all,
please make yourselves at home.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:37.940
Thank you, Captain.
But is this really going to work?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:44.320
The youngsters on board this ship
just don’t look like they’re up to battle…

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:49.410
If battles could be won on the basis
of looks alone, I would abide by that.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:54.380
But the Simoun sibyllae
are the mainstay of our nation.

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.790
That is an undeniable fact.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:00.890
All sides are watching as we
launch this historical campaign.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:02.670
There will be no room for failure.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.670
First and foremost, I believe it is
important that we trust each other.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:11.180
Yes, you’re probably right.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:15.200
Then we’ve agreed
to go through with this?

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.870
Of course.
We’re counting on you too.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:19.130
Very well.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.690
Explain, Dominüra.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.400
We’re about to form
a united front with these soldiers.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:32.220
We’re counting on you, Sibylla…

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:33.950
It’s Neviril.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.410
Sibylla Neviril.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.070
A united front?

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:47.170
Yes, it seems we’ll be joining
forces with those men somehow.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.440
Us?

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:50.680
With those people?

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.730
Sibylla, you’re so sweet!

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:01.690
We’re being dragged
down further and further.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.420
What’ll become of us?

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:08.690
Well, a cramped ship getting
more cramped is a problem.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:12.390
Some people seem
to be enjoying themselves.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:17.270
Oh, for real?
You’re from around here.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.770
Yes, I enlisted as
soon as this war began.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:23.420
Good for you. You’re an ally of justice.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:26.170
Then as a reward,
I’ll show you around this ship.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.110
What’s wrong?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.680
Uh, you see…
I shouldn’t be touching a sibylla…

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:35.760
It won’t make any difference.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:40.520
We haven’t gone to the Spring yet,
but that’s the only difference.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.930
Don’t worry… I’m going
to become a woman anyway.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.530
T-That’s not what I meant…

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:53.060
Under normal circumstances,
a lowly enlisted man like me…

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:55.370
…wouldn’t dare speak to a priestess…

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:59.540
I told you not
to make things so complicated!

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:00.830
Let’s go!

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.890
The last few weeks,
enemy attacks have increased…

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:11.950
…leaving us no choice but
to fall back from our defense lines.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:16.660
To keep the enemy from gaining more
ground, we’ll launch an operation…

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:21.310
…to reclaim this town here,
Urvel, their apparent target.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:25.130
It’ll go down like this.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:29.010
First, we’ll transport our troops
by using the Simoun planes.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:30.820
Transport? Us?

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:36.150
Yes, we’ll outfit the Simouns with
special transport armor to do it.

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.330
The Simouns will transport soldiers?

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:43.330
If there were another way, we’d do it.
Can you try to understand?

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:53.390
The soldiers aboard will be deployed
to secret posts around the city.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:09:00.310
After which the main battalion
will push forward on my signal.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.980
We’ll launch a pincer attack
and destroy the enemy.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:07.680
What else do you wish us to do?

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:13.360
Leave the rest to us. Once you’ve
transported us, your job is done.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:18.620
The operation will start the night
of the new moon, tomorrow at 2300.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:22.390
Make sure you’re all
in top form for this task.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.620
Right.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:25.750
What?

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:29.080
How could they do such
a thing to the Simouns?

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:35.210
I’m not doing this to our divine
aircraft because I want to either.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:39.090
No way! Don’t you feel
bad for the Simouns?

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.600
And that thing…

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:46.670
To tell you the truth, it’s so lame!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.520
I’m telling you…

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.030
The other day,
we were flying over the ocean.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:58.660
And we saw this huge fish, and I
thought, “That looks pretty tasty.”

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.030
You can tell she couldn’t
care less about the rest of us.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:05.670
The way she’s just about
throwing herself at him…

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:08.960
Well, we might not be that different.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:14.050
When your back’s to the wall, there’s
no time to think of others’ feelings.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:18.810
In an ideal world, we’d all
learn to understand each other…

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:20.740
…just like those two.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.290
Is it good?

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.810
Yes, quite delicious.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:28.140
Delicious?

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.520
Well, I’m glad to hear it.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:43.000
I can see I’ve been mistaken
about sibyllae all along.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.100
Mistaken?

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:49.920
Yes, I thought sibyllae were holier,
those whom must never be violated…

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.920
I thought you didn’t talk much.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.310
Are you disillusioned?

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:58.650
No, totally the opposite!

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:02.130
Because I’m talking to you like this.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:04.140
Yeah, I’m glad too.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.900
Floe.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:16.770
What is it?

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.940
I hear you’re friendly with a soldier.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.310
Yes, his name is Mastiff.

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:23.370
Keep your standing in mind.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.410
Standing?

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:28.150
We are priestesses
serving Tempus Spatium.

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:30.450
Indiscretions should be avoided.

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:33.420
That kind of talk’s
so behind the times.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:36.170
I can’t help it. I like him.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:39.960
Floe, I said you
shouldn’t say things like that…

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:42.870
We’ll all go to
the Spring sooner or later.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:45.400
Then sibylla or soldier won’t matter.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.180
Listen, Floe…

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.980
Jeez, I’ll just quit being a sibylla then!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.690
Then it won’t be a problem, right?

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:53.900
Floe!

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:02.650
What a headache…

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:23.880
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:30.040
Still, is it all right?

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:32.620
Yes, it’s fine. Did I keep you waiting?

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:33.710
No.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:36.020
Really, Mastiff! You’re so sweet!

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:38.520
Don’t you want to get close?

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:40.360
It’s not that…

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.540
Then…

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:52.530
Sibylla Floe, you and
the others serve Tempus Spatium…

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:54.570
…and are closest to God.

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:57.040
I guess. Where did that come from?

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:00.850
We too harbor
deep religious convictions.

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:04.650
But rather than out of love
and respect for Tempus Spatium…

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:07.550
…it’s because we couldn’t
go on if we didn’t believe.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.790
What do you think of
this war we’re fighting?

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:18.060
I don’t like it. But we’ve
got to fight or we’ll be killed.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.440
How do you feel about killing people?

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:33.410
Then why did you enlist?

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:39.730
I can’t really explain it,
but everyone else enlisted…

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:45.910
Tomorrow’s operation is a campaign
to reclaim the city where I was born.

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:52.040
Mornings are very beautiful in Urvel.

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:59.270
Especially the view from the top of
the tower in the center of the city…

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.690
It’s beyond compare.

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:04.660
That’s why I…

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:16.410
It’ll be all right, Mastiff.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.080
Because I’ll protect you.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.570
Begin the operation!

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:51.200
Let’s go, men!
By the grace of Tempus Spatium!

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.740
By the grace!

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:21.730
We’ll fly as close to the ground as
possible. Stay out of enemy sight.

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:27.730
We are banning Ri Majons till further
notice to avoid damaging facilities.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:32.790
After transport, disengage
containers and retreat northwest.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:33.950
Understood?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:35.240
Yes, sir!

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:44.960
Simoun sibyllae,
we pray for your safe return.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:58.180
I have to say they’ve become ugly.

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:00.890
I can’t wait to get rid of these things.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:04.600
It’s hard not to drop them.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:09.110
Yeah… I just hope Mastiff
doesn’t run into any danger.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:13.370
Roatreamon,
that hairstyle of yours is so lovely.

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:14.860
Thank you, Morinas.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.700
We’ll see more of these.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:21.500
Rimone, this is a pivotal operation,
a springboard for future missions.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.210
You’ll understand soon enough.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.960
So this is a front-line mission…

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.890
We’re almost at
the drop-off point, Paraietta.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:36.720
Right.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:23.710
So we’re done already?

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:26.510
That was a pretty quick operation.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.740
I’ll undock the containers.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:31.400
So you didn’t like those things either.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:36.670
I guess. It’s asking too much to even
pretend to like such awkward…

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:41.890
What’s this…

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:44.190
Flares. Have they spotted us?

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:48.420
No, from the number, we should
assume it was a trap from the start.

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:52.550
Not good. If so, then those
old guys will get ambushed!

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:55.880
We’ll go support them.
Understood, Aer?

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:12.540
They set us up.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:29.460
Everyone, retreat!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:30.630
Yes, sir!

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:50.030
Hey, they may be ugly,
but they can be useful.

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:51.520
We’ll keep up support.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.560
Okay.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:57.670
See that? We’ve got
holy priestesses on our side!

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:00.260
Step it up, guys!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:10.420
That’s right, Rimone… Keep going…

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:11.880
Just keep going!

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.380
Just keep going?

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.880
What are you doing? Fire, Floe!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.960
Mastiff… Where’s Mastiff?

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:23.000
Floe!

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:25.390
Please, Alty, try to find him!

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:27.330
We don’t have time.

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:28.480
Please!

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.860
What’s wrong, Kaim? Fire!

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.010
Kaim!

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:44.740
But, Para-sama…

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:47.540
I can see…
I can see people down there!

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:53.000
Pull it together. Don’t dare bring any
more dishonor to the priestesses!

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:04.470
Neviril, at this rate, they’ll…

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.850
A Ri Majon. Strike with a Ri Majon.

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:11.100
I know. But a Ri Majon
would unleash too much force.

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:15.160
Will you stand by and
let those men die, Neviril?

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.370
The Ri Majon ban is lifted.

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:35.370
Floe, the Iron Ri Majon!

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:38.600
We can’t! If we do,
it’ll put Mastiff in danger!

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:40.330
His city will be…

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:41.880
If we don’t, he’ll die anyway!

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:46.490
Floe!

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:52.850
All right.

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:55.280
This is a Ri Majon’s power?

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:58.360
Amazing… It’s like ten tanks at once.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.450
We can make it…
We can make it now!

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.200
Target is city plaza,
the enemy command center!

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.830
Iron Ri Majon!

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.000
Stop!

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:12.830
I want…

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.830
I want to protect Mastiff.

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:20.380
To protect Mastiff!

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:30.710
They did it!

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:33.650
They blew up
the enemy command center!

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:43.230
Could they really be
Tempus Spatium sibyllae…

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:44.320
Simouns…

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:48.830
Could that be Floe?

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:52.810
All right! The priestesses
have cleared the way for us!

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:54.880
Let’s show what we’re made of!

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:55.830
Right!

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:00.800
This battle… No…

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:04.300
They can’t be divine aircraft…

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:07.380
They’re…

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:08.800
The Simouns are…

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:11.810
The Simouns are demons!

00:22:13.020 --> 00:22:15.230
Mastiff, what are you doing?

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:19.060
You can’t let children like that
take part in a war anymore!

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:22.260
This war is ours to fight!

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:47.860
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.860 --> 00:22:52.100
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:59.140
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:06.700
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:19.620
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:24.830
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:28.840
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:32.780
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:38.720
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:44.260
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.260 --> 00:23:47.690
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:53.360
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:59.590
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.590
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:11.470
Kaim and Alty have taken off on
a reconnaissance mission as a pair.

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:15.430
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:19.930
<b>Sisters</b>

00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:18.100
Sisters.
